-- title:
--   Natural process filtration is monotone in observation horizon
-- statement:
--   The sigma-field generated by observations of a process up to an earlier nonnegative time s is contained in that generated up to any later time t≥s. The published Chapter 1 definition naturalSigma X t is definitionally PerfCorrMSQ.natFiltr X t, an iSup over observation times u≤t of comap sigma-fields, so each generator present at s is also present at t. This exact algebraic inclusion is needed to lift rational-time crossing events from a shorter horizon to any fixed future observation horizon when proving first-passage stopping-time measurability.
-- source:
--   Kyprianou (2006), Chapter 1 first-passage natural-filtration formalisation.

import Definitions.Def_Kyprianou_Ch01_McKeanBrownianStopping
import Definitions.Def_PerfCorrMSQ_NaturalFiltration
open Kyprianou.Ch01
open scoped NNReal
set_option autoImplicit false

theorem Kyprianou.Ch01.naturalSigma_monotone
    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω]
    (X : ℝ≥0 → Ω → ℝ) {s t : ℝ≥0} (hst : s ≤ t) :
    Kyprianou.Ch01.naturalSigma X s ≤ Kyprianou.Ch01.naturalSigma X t := by sorry
